p.src:
A four-vector is an object that transforms as a spacetime displacement does. To make that definition useful, first recall the transformations of the coordinates themselves. For a boost of speed $v$ in the $x$-direction, $\begin{aligned}
  x'&=\gamma(x-vt), & y'&=y, & z'&=z,
  & t'&=\gamma(t-vx),                                      \end{aligned}$ where $\gamma(v)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-v^2}}.$

