p.src:
For each spatial component, $U^i=\frac{dx^i}{d\tau}
     =\frac{dx^i}{dt}\frac{dt}{d\tau}
     =v^i\frac{dt}{d\tau}.$ Divide Eq.  by $dt^2$: $\left(\frac{d\tau}{dt}\right)^2
  =1-v_x^2-v_y^2-v_z^2
  =1-\boldsymbol v^2.$ Therefore $\frac{dt}{d\tau}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-\boldsymbol v^2}}
  =\gamma(\lvert\boldsymbol v\rvert),$ and $U^\mu=(\gamma v_x,\gamma v_y,\gamma v_z,\gamma).$

